[00:08.58]1. At the start of the day, with the sun yet to rise,
[00:17.06]We are making our way
[00:19.22]with the sleep in our eyes, and we pray.
[00:25.46]We are there with a smile for the people we meet.
[00:33.86]Some may stop for a while,
[00:35.78]some pass by on the street, but we stay.
[00:42.30](Chorus)
[00:42.30]It’s the life that we choose;
[00:46.56]For Jehovah we live.
[00:50.44]And whatever he asks, we will do.
[00:59.28]In the work we endure,
[01:02.84]Whether sunshine or rain.
[01:07.22]It’s a way we can say ev’ry day: “I love you.”
[01:24.40]2. At the end of the day, with the sun sinking low,
[01:33.04]Feeling happy and tired,
[01:34.72]in our heart there’s a glow, and we pray.
[01:41.21]It’s a life that we love, always giving our best.
[01:49.87]And Jehovah we thank,
[01:51.63]for by him we are blessed ev’ry day.
[01:57.53](Chorus)
[01:58.09]It’s the life that we choose;
[02:01.89]For Jehovah we live.
[02:06.15]And whatever he asks, we will do.
[02:14.97]In the work we endure,
[02:18.73]Whether sunshine or rain.
[02:23.07]It’s a way we can say ev’ry day: “I love you.”
